523	    /** Move the claim to {@code next}; refused when the user's role may not open, settle or void it (see
524	     * {@link SettingsService#allowed}), and when its current status does not allow it (a PENDING
525	     * claim can only be voided here: it is approved or rejected instead). Settling it fixes what is due
526	     * on it then (the figure it is bound to, when a statement bound it, otherwise its person's rate then)
527	     * together with its late charge then (none on a correction); the user who opened it cannot settle it,
528	     * and a clerk's settle of it when that due is above the sheet's clerk limit (a due that is n/a is
529	     * within any limit) leaves it PENDING instead, fixing nothing, until a steward approves or rejects
530	     * it. A claim deferred on the sheet's today cannot be settled, nor one without proofs whose due is
531	     * above the proof threshold in force on its date (refused before the clerk limit is considered). A
532	     * SETTLED claim can only be voided by a steward, and only while the sheet's today is at most 7 days
533	     * after its settlement (its status log's SETTLED date); its frozen figure then leaves every total and
534	     * is recorded as reversed. A voided claim keeps its number, if it had one. */
535	    @Transactional
536	    public Claim changeStatus(String sheetId, String user, long claimId, ClaimStatus next) {
537	        return changeStatus(sheetId, user, claimId, next, null);
538	    }
